# The optional set for Bill Autopilot, staged on top of the minimal one.
#
# One line per mod: packageId, then its Workshop id. `#` starts a comment. `first:` in front of a
# packageId activates it ahead of everything else; nothing here needs that, because the order that
# matters is the one About.xml already declares in <loadAfter> and the staging honours it.
#
# Every packageId below was read out of that mod's own About.xml on 2026-09-21, never from its
# Workshop title: three of these seven are continuations whose title and packageId disagree, and
# guessing one makes the staging die before anything runs.
#
# Order matters twice here, so the lines are not alphabetical:
#   - Nice Bill Tab - Expansion extends Nice Bill Tab and comes after it.
#   - No Max Bills: Redux is what raises the per-bench bill ceiling that Better Workbench
#     Management then reports, so it goes ahead of BWM.
#
# This mod depends on none of them. All six it declares in <loadAfter> are covered, plus one that
# it does not declare and does not reach: No Max Bills. It is here because it changes a number the
# mod is documented to honour - the bill ceiling goes from 15 to 125 - and 10-bill-cap.feature
# reads that ceiling live rather than hard-coding 15, so this pass is where the raised one is
# actually exercised.
#
#   justharry.nomaxbillsredux    the raised bill ceiling; 10 reads it live
#   falconne.BWM                 13 - the largest bridge, and the one with no witness at all. It
#                                prefixes BillStack.Delete to erase what it attached to a bill, and
#                                the autopilot removes and re-places bills constantly
#   Andromeda.NiceBillTab        15 - the cached row list, and the drag that can resurrect a bill
#   HICON.NiceBillTabExpansion   17 - hidden recipes
#   Dubwise.DubsMintMenus        16 - bench templates, which photograph every bill on a bench
#   Memegoddess.EverybodyGetsOne 14 - a repeat mode belonging to another mod
#   zal.chooseyourrecipe         no scenario of its own: it removes disabled recipes from the
#                                workbench itself, so the autopilot never sees them and there is
#                                nothing of this mod's to assert. Staged anyway, because "it
#                                changes nothing here" is a claim, and this pass is where the rest
#                                of the suite stays green beside it or does not
#
# ONE SET, not several. The doctrine wants a named set per exclusive combination, so the question
# had to be answered before writing this file: Nice Bill Tab redraws the whole bills tab, Better
# Workbench Management adds to it, and Dubs Mint Menus keeps its own menu beside it.
#
# Virginie, who plays with these, has seen no incompatibility between them (2026-09-21). That is
# the best evidence available and it is what this single set rests on - it is a player's experience,
# not a measurement, which is exactly why the pass exists. A scenario going red here because two
# neighbours fight is a real result, and the answer to it is to split this file into one named set
# per combination rather than to widen a tolerance.
#
# packageId                     workshopId   what it is
justharry.nomaxbillsredux       3526216885   No Max Bills: Redux
falconne.BWM                    935982361    Better Workbench Management
Andromeda.NiceBillTab           3520130671   Nice Bill Tab
HICON.NiceBillTabExpansion      3721023311   Nice Bill Tab - Expansion
Dubwise.DubsMintMenus           1446523594   Dubs Mint Menus
Memegoddess.EverybodyGetsOne    3530806680   Everybody Gets One - Continued
zal.chooseyourrecipe            3263007587   Choose Your Recipe (Continued)
